(a) Besides sexual contact with an infected person, HIV and Hepatitis-B are transmitted by (any two):
- **sharing injection needles or surgical instruments** with an infected person;
- **transfusion of blood** contaminated with the virus;
- from an **infected mother to the foetus** through the placenta.

(b) Early detection is essential so that the infected person gets **proper treatment** in time, before the disease causes serious complications, and so that **further spread** of the infection to healthy people is prevented. Many such infections show few or no symptoms in the early stages, so without detection a person can unknowingly pass them on.
